<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <Version>3.1.0</Version>
    <Authors>Steve Hatchett</Authors>
    <Description>C# library to support text and person name fuzzy matching. Contains Levenshtein and Damerau-Levenshtein (optimal string alignment) edit distance and normalized similarity functions optimized for speed and reduced memory consumption, including bounded max-distance and min-similarity variants.</Description>
    <Copyright>Copyright © 2015-2026 Steve Hatchett</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/softwx/SoftWx.Match</PackageProjectUrl>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/softwx/SoftWx.Match</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>v3.1.0
- Added ReadOnlySpan&lt;char&gt; default interface methods to IDistance and ISimilarity on .NET 8+ without breaking existing implementers
- Improved single-algorithm source copyability: moved CharSpan/IntSpan aliases to per-file #if NET8_0_OR_GREATER directives (making SpanShim.cs netstandard2.0-only) and split Distance/Similarity into partial classes alongside Levenshtein.cs and DamerauOSA.cs
- Switched instance and netstandard2.0 thread-local scratch buffers to geometric growth from a 32-element minimum to avoid repeated reallocations on varying word lengths
- Hardened netstandard2.0 IntSpan.Slice to reject nonzero start offsets in Release builds as well as Debug
- Added Debug test runs and standalone single-algorithm copyability checks to CI, and documented direct file-copying and ordinal/normalization behavior in README

v3.0.2
- Added internal netstandard2.0 span shim (zero-overhead ReadOnlySpan&lt;char&gt;/Span&lt;int&gt; aliases on net8.0+) to unify DP algorithms and helper paths across target frameworks
- Consolidated duplicated fast-path, Similarity, and static facade logic, cutting library code size by ~28% and eliminating mid-method #if directives while preserving net8.0+ performance
- Minor internal code cleanup and benchmark setup deduplication

v3.0.1
- Updated copyright attribution, and added SPDX-License-Identifier headers
- Updated blog links to HTTPS
- Added consumer-level NativeAOT publish and execution smoke test in CI/Release

v3.0.0
- Multi-targeted for netstandard2.0, net8.0, and net10.0 (dropped netstandard1.0)
- Enabled nullable reference types, trimming/NativeAOT compatibility, and built-in Source Link
- Added ReadOnlySpan&lt;char&gt; overloads (net8.0+), zero-allocation static methods (stackalloc/ArrayPool on net8.0+, capped thread-local cache on netstandard2.0), capped instance buffer retention, lazy maxDistance initialization, SIMD CommonPrefixLength, and O(1) fast paths
- Fixed Similarity returning 1.0 when one string is a prefix or suffix of the other
- Fixed inverted null handling in Similarity.DamerauOSA and Helpers.NullSimilarityResults
- Fixed fractional and NaN maxDistance handling in Levenshtein.Distance and DamerauOSA.Distance
- Added missing ISimilarity interface declaration to DamerauOSA</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <PackageTags>levenshtein;damerau;damerau-levenshtein;edit-distance;similarity;matching;fuzzy;softwx</PackageTags>

    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <IsTrimmable Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsTargetFrameworkCompatible('$(TargetFramework)', 'net6.0'))">true</IsTrimmable>
    <IsAotCompatible Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsTargetFrameworkCompatible('$(TargetFramework)', 'net8.0'))">true</IsAotCompatible>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
